      "family": "Controlled Qualification",
      "hash": "594d1861f288aaefb98e51a8222a1ab4e84743c06655b95fcd32ba6e9eb8d2c9",
      "id": "ap:emission-without-validation",
      "label": "AP-01",
      "source": "corpus/canon/resources/anti-patterns.md",
      "start": 7,
      "text": "### AP-01. emission-without-validation\n\nDetect: A technique's Protocol instruction or Rules clause explicitly directs an artifact's emission without validating that artifact first. Review each instruction and each semicolon-separated clause independently. Validation elsewhere does not excuse an instruction or clause that explicitly permits unvalidated emission.\n\nDo not flag: A directive to validate before emission satisfies this criterion. A heading, output declaration, retention clause, destination declaration, routine call, binding or graph label does not itself direct emission. Capability descriptions describe the service and are not imperative instructions.\n\nFix: Require validation of the same artifact before emission in every emitting instruction and clause.\n",
      "title": "AP-01. emission-without-validation"
    }
  },
